  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-02T22:17:46.679Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So this is the fourth time I've been \"vote kicked\" from a map called \"The Snooze's Scary Maze 4\" for doing absolutely nothing wrong and just wandering through the maze with a few friends. I've checked the user list the past three times (there's always been 20+ players on the world when I get randomly kicked) and I've figured out who's doing it because they're the only one that's been online in the instance during all four occurrences of such happening. I've reported the offending user for harassment but aside from that I'm not sure what else to do to prevent this from happening. Every day when I try to play on that world the user in question kicks me for no reason. I'll see them hanging around in spawn, and after I've been in the maze for about a half an hour I'll just get kicked and sent back to my home world with a message saying more than half the players in the world voted to kick me.\n\nThere needs to be a way to see when a vote kick is being cast upon you, and a way for you to see who started the vote. There also needs to be a limit applied to how quickly you're allowed to vote kick people to prevent someone from spamming a vote kick until enough people get fed up with the notification and click accept just to stop it from popping up again. I have no doubt in my mind that's what's going on, and it needs to stop. People who abuse the privilege to vote kick other people should lose that right indefinitely.",
